#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129892} :activity/id #uuid "87e23de1-746c-5124-9751-bee5befcb28f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048554 :topic/id #uuid "a93bb5a8-5344-5f11-a0fd-45410668ecd6" :topic/math-academy-id 1984} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129892 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130327 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we will learn how to compute the tangent plane to the level surface $f (x, y, z) = k,$ where $k$ is a constant, at some point $\\mathbf x_0 = (x_0, y_0, z_0).$ \n\nAs an example, consider the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = x^2 +y^2+z.\n$$\n\n \n\nSuppose that we wish to find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=  (1,1, 2).$ \n\nEvaluating $f$ at the point $(1,1,2),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = (1)^2 +(1)^2+2 = 4.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the equation of our level surface is\n\n$$\nx^2 +y^2+z = 4.\n$$\n\nNow, to find the equation of the tangent plane to this surface at $(1,1,2),$ we can use the following result:\n\n  *Given a hypersurface $w = f(x,y,z)$ and a point $\\mathbf x_0 = (x_0,y_0,z_0)$ that lies in the domain of $f$, the gradient $\\nabla \\! f (\\mathbf x_0)$ is normal to the tangent plane of the level surface $f (x, y, z) = k$ at the point $\\mathbf x_0$*. \n\n![](images/11/1140e80fbb2efd684311cb7625e5b0be361d6fb951036253f57b9e51234de3ee.png)\n\n       \n\nWe can now find the equation of the tangent plane to our level surface.\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $\\mathbf x_0 = (1,1,2)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}\\,i+{f}_{y}\\,j+{f}_{z}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j+k \\\\ ∇f(1,1,2) & =2(1)\\text{ }i+2(1)\\text{ }j+k \\\\  & =2\\text{ }i+2\\text{ }j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally,  we write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\nabla f(x_0,y_0,z_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0, \\: z-z_0 \\rangle & = 0 \\[3pt]\n\\nabla f(1,1,2) \\cdot \\langle x-1, \\: y-1, \\: z-2 \\rangle & = 0 \\[3pt]\n\\langle 2,\\:2,\\:1\\rangle\\cdot \\langle x-1, y-1, z-2\\rangle &= 0\\[3pt]\n      2(x-1)+ 2(y-1) + (z-2) & =0\\\n      2x +2y +z -6&=0   \n}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "7f7db883-9d6e-5a67-97d4-20274467a1e2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2500 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "13f10d0e-ddd7-5833-b73f-b3f00ff7016a" :step/math-academy-id 11201 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129893}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129893 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128893 :question/id #uuid "09499f38-a497-5f59-9cb2-0882a5853320" :question/math-academy-id "e-3368"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050027}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129596} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129598} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323793} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348447} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348448} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348449} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366808} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366815} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394071} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475921} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475937} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475970} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493943} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554582} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554584}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"} :step/id #uuid "6d9d3ca6-ae9b-5ac5-a35f-80fa6628ef2f" :step/math-academy-id 11204 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130048}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186130048 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128998 :question/id #uuid "9091e2dc-5b05-5ae7-a498-9de0483ec375" :question/math-academy-id "e-6183"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129600} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129611} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237932} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237933} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323850} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348450} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348452} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354471} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368502} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368852} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475928} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475932} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475934} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554541} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554623}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"} :step/id #uuid "f4dac68d-5f9a-5fba-b2c5-3ea5a9ec6475" :step/math-academy-id 23124}] :activity/title "Tangent Planes to Level Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186129332}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494072} :activity/id #uuid "63e75d2f-a87d-5228-8980-4d6f3fc9a47a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048554 :topic/id #uuid "a93bb5a8-5344-5f11-a0fd-45410668ecd6" :topic/math-academy-id 1984} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494023 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c75f8c9-6d90-5e2f-9fd0-6d4f8cbd173a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,e,2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+2,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493465} {:answer/id #uuid "3050b9e4-da08-5715-ad5a-8caf10a32624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,-e,-2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493472} {:answer/id #uuid "472c72f7-428a-5c92-9b64-36649f199a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e,1,2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493511} {:answer/id #uuid "67d37bdf-2be9-5b4b-b6fd-993f6357958d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,e,-2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493545} {:answer/id #uuid "a09c4894-0619-505a-853a-743d133d9d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,e,-e⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+2,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493645}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493472} :answer-field/id #uuid "49ccc9b7-9d2d-5fab-9305-0a2ddb6c4989" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a1c45efd-b454-595e-a933-aae318d15f95" :question/math-academy-id "q-102700" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}\\text{ }i-{e}^{z}\\text{ }j-y{e}^{z}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,2,1) & =\\frac{2}{1}\\text{ }i-{e}^{1}\\text{ }j-(2){e}^{1}k \\\\  & =2\\,i-e\\,j-2ek \\\\  & =⟨2,-e,-2e⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,-e,-2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7ecf0ade-c143-56c2-83e7-b60005d8d75d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494028}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494027 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8438dc-a715-5c0c-aab2-6e47f02ae119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x-y+2z-10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236008} {:answer/id #uuid "85b07a3f-7374-5a9c-b7c1-947842c86d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x+3y+z+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236650} {:answer/id #uuid "94a5b114-54d1-55a1-b257-cc17cc5b9faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-y+5z-12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236759} {:answer/id #uuid "b02e51c4-263c-5a4d-80f9-9315bea2d383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+4y-3z+15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236937} {:answer/id #uuid "c93bc415-579e-5faf-ba97-c8c120703f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x+4y+5z-18=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237093}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237093} :answer-field/id #uuid "86e7ba58-6e3b-5d46-8ec2-848013d679c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a47eb1cf-14ab-540e-8110-7aec36247dcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-102711" :question/problem "Consider the surface $xy{z}^{2}=6-z.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(1,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy{z}^{2} & =6-z \\\\ xy{z}^{2}+z & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+z$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=6.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(y{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+(x{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+(2xyz+1)\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,2) & =(1)(2)^{2}\\text{ }i+(1)(2)^{2}\\text{ }j+(2(1)(1)(2)+1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i+4j+5\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,4,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,2)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,4,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)+4(y-1)+5(z-2) & =0 \\\\ 4x+4y+5z-18 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8542cb45-fe3e-585c-beae-8f3803d3fd88"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494028 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193c9497-7ea6-5a1d-b9f5-a009ce93ca23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x-y+12z-24=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366817} {:answer/id #uuid "f29eacee-8051-57cb-aee4-51b137c18ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x-y+z+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366818} {:answer/id #uuid "710265a2-6141-5b27-8548-bda3797d8905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x-2y-5z+11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366819} {:answer/id #uuid "d24d01c2-6eb5-5662-b203-5deae9c0dd73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x-3y-4z+24=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366820} {:answer/id #uuid "8c31a377-21c2-5c10-92eb-4e6439b5d5dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-y-4z+13=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366821}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366817} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac4c269d-3ccc-505a-8b3b-1f9e614487fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "baefe5d5-6705-561e-af37-627a61278732" :question/math-academy-id "q-102704" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(\\frac{1}{2},3,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(\\frac{1}{2},3,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =12x\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j+3{z}^{2}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(\\frac{1}{2},3,2) & =12\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j+3(2)^{2}k \\\\  & =6\\,i-\\,j+12k \\\\  & =⟨6,-1,12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(\\frac{1}{2},3,2)\\cdot ⟨x-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y-3,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨6,-1,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y-3,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6(x-\\frac{1}{2})-(y-3)+12(z-2) & =0 \\\\ 6x-y+12z-24 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "867c6d88-e80e-5619-af3d-96e820e79d18" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494027}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494051 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28cd2801-6575-503c-8973-e5d77533e487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-2y+2z-8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321465} {:answer/id #uuid "740d2fc5-1db2-531b-9591-8ebbee71f486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-4y+z+6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322054} {:answer/id #uuid "adb3e2fe-6b96-5d2f-a240-7193b0f2a939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-y+z-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322509} {:answer/id #uuid "c2da99c8-1b83-5384-b154-4692549ce45c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+2y-2z-12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322659} {:answer/id #uuid "c69134c6-e59d-5120-8af3-0b8bb7f8b190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-2y+2z+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322687}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186322687} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e18b7a8-1caf-5bbf-be09-d1d09a6d4c0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1c6c7087-87b2-59e1-b5dd-8db545cc6eaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-36765" :question/problem "Consider the surface ${x}^{2}=-xyz.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(4,2,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =-xyz \\\\ {x}^{2}+xyz & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xyz$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(4,2,-2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2x+yz)\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(4,2,-2) & =(2(4)+2(-2))\\text{ }i+4(-2)\\text{ }j+4(2)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i-8j+8\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,-8,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(4,2,-2)\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-2,\\,z+2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,-8,8⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-2,\\,z+2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-4)+(-8)(y-2)+8(z+2) & =0 \\\\ 4x-8y+8z+16 & =0 \\\\ x-2y+2z+4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b8b241c5-9ed0-5065-b6d8-8a3dd561fd54" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494023}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494072 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129596 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13a034a0-40db-53e2-8743-0500f64927fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-e,\\,y-e,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493426} {:answer/id #uuid "4d8e49ba-c572-585b-9000-22f731c9e31c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493516} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd70068-b6fc-58b5-a8fd-0b6d0f6cdc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493590} {:answer/id #uuid "a4259989-16f4-5162-93ea-522cff1adbaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,1,e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493652} {:answer/id #uuid "b48376c2-fa7d-5ea7-a3f5-9c2f64a3454e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1,\\,z+e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493683}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493516} :answer-field/id #uuid "675858d2-09f1-5094-a85f-2db7923cff6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "39528896-10e8-5126-bdec-f26e9bdcc487" :question/math-academy-id "q-36334" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{y}-z$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,e).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,1,e):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\text{ }i+x{e}^{y}\\text{ }j-k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,e) & ={e}^{1}\\text{ }i+(1){e}^{1}\\text{ }j-k \\\\  & =e\\,i+e\\,j-k \\\\  & =⟨e,e,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,e)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f7e115a4-0109-5dcd-be67-0eff6d8c34d2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494051}}] :activity/title "Tangent Planes to Level Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493376}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554682} :activity/id #uuid "9ef07479-9bd3-50f2-b4da-e02ee5217b48" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048554 :topic/id #uuid "a93bb5a8-5344-5f11-a0fd-45410668ecd6" :topic/math-academy-id 1984} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554672 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554623 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "003c768f-4220-5a83-901d-9287c7398508" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553864} {:answer/id #uuid "189491e7-f8db-50dd-a6d1-6eeaca6515ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e-2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553914} {:answer/id #uuid "c65e5475-456e-5a45-8351-be33d7aba2f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554305} {:answer/id #uuid "d5390bff-ed73-5aab-86b6-9bd0d5dc8156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554334} {:answer/id #uuid "f88cff99-c81a-54d6-be8d-ad3057aab4a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554407}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553864} :answer-field/id #uuid "d777c8fd-8f4e-5ca8-a5be-b50636868cd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d5913a4b-d974-52bc-82fc-74c4bb66f8ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-102710" :question/problem "Consider the surface ${e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}=e-3.$ Given that $n=⟨a,b,c⟩$ is a non-zero normal vector to the surface at the point $(1,1,-1),$ what is the value of $\\frac{a-b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define  $f(x,y,z)={e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}.$ Then, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=e-3.$  \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2}))j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{xy}-{x}^{2}-2{z}^{2})k \\\\  & =(y{e}^{xy}-2x)i+(x{e}^{xy})j+(-4z)k \\\\ ∇f(1,1,-1) & =((1){e}^{(1)(1)}-2(1))\\text{ }i+(1){e}^{(1)(1)}\\text{ }j+(-4)(-1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(e-2)\\text{ }i+e\\text{ }j+4\\text{ }k \\\\  & =⟨e-2,\\,e,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩=⟨e-2,\\,e,\\,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a-b}{c}=\\frac{(e-2)-e}{4}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "48086a64-8671-5a00-bbb5-b58661fd7a59" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554715}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554677 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366808 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9d90141-bb87-557b-8f42-7d42bba3c91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x+2y+4z-16=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366810} {:answer/id #uuid "152ddd87-e22d-58da-85bb-b549e713fa60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x+4y+3z-10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366811} {:answer/id #uuid "e03a5aca-94df-508f-a37f-bf286cd93f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-3y+z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366812} {:answer/id #uuid "e48a7bda-ef25-5ea3-836f-2a4b00051777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5x+y+2z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366813} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b69228-be90-5f3b-83c0-2b8ff34eb2da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-2y+z-9=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366814}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366810} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab905e04-ebcb-5bbc-8e7d-cdb57e6bb24a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "843be179-016c-55ad-bf04-357dd9b69f33" :question/math-academy-id "q-102701" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=xyz-{z}^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,3,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+(xy-2z)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,3,1) & =(3)(1)\\text{ }i+2(1)\\text{ }j+(2(3)-2(1))k \\\\  & =3\\,i+2\\,j+4k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,3,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨3,2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3(x-2)+2(y-3)+4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 3x+2y+4z-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "588c4361-50c9-5029-a566-867e8863cbe8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554672}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554682 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55726bdf-bd92-5f7e-a7bc-7a1d0597e754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394073} {:answer/id #uuid "9575e423-448b-5b5c-91fc-c2a7c6afcec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394074} {:answer/id #uuid "21a4639b-6da9-5a98-9ba9-dde732cd477b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y+2,\\,z-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394075} {:answer/id #uuid "14d65a68-8209-56ec-85e3-86c5087733e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394076} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd689ee-da18-5ee8-8e2e-94f4eb0e8982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨3,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394077}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394073} :answer-field/id #uuid "1883a36c-4cc8-545f-9348-6c077cb4b1e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6f18a33a-3190-5d7a-b7c8-c7f2c7cbfe22" :question/math-academy-id "q-80768" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz$,  find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,-1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,-1,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2xy-z)\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2y)\\text{ }j-xk \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-1,-1) & =(\\,2(2)(-1)-(-1)\\,)\\text{ }i+(\\,{2}^{2}+2(-1)\\,)\\text{ }j-2k \\\\  & =-3\\,i+2\\,j-2\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,-1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7191b9bd-5ed6-54dc-8494-3debf9947402" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554749}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554715 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065677e5-6668-589c-8f82-28615b7c7eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-6y+z-13=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553881} {:answer/id #uuid "8da732bc-eb58-5338-abe0-8d52e81e25e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x+8y-5z+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554168} {:answer/id #uuid "bd87e438-6635-5fc8-8041-e85ff749d4dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x+9y-z+16=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554281} {:answer/id #uuid "d50bfffc-a66c-5b56-a37e-a72964286f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x+5y-6z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554332} {:answer/id #uuid "ea005b66-1e1f-575c-a788-5fbfb346d025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x+8y-6z+30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554379}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554379} :answer-field/id #uuid "74e95cce-259a-58bc-a6dc-cf74c51c993b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "138bcf11-9efc-57ee-ad7b-ef21818db0e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-102712" :question/problem "Consider the surface ${z}^{2}y+16=4\\sqrt{x}+y.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(4,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}y+16 & =4\\sqrt{x}+y. \\\\ {z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)={z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-16.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(4,-1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}y-4\\sqrt{x}-y)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}\\text{ }i+({z}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+2zy\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(4,-1,3) & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4}}\\text{ }i+({3}^{2}-1)\\text{ }j+2(3)(-1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =-\\,i+8\\text{ }j-6\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-1,8,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(4,-1,3)\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y+1,\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,8,-6⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y+1,\\,z-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -(x-4)+8(y+1)-6(z-3) & =0 \\\\ -x+8y-6z+30 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9ee2cdbe-40de-5a18-809a-b2ba9fbc04a8"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554749 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554584 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1038e636-38ca-52da-90c5-a091da531eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2ex+2ey+\\frac{z}{e}-4e+\\frac{1}{e}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553902} {:answer/id #uuid "27782ffe-f397-5d41-939c-10588c08a068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2ex-2ey-\\frac{z}{e}-\\frac{1}{e}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553943} {:answer/id #uuid "8605bb25-4120-54e0-870c-c12a2d8a2246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2ex+2ey+\\frac{z}{e}-2e+\\frac{1}{e}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554145} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a1e914-b611-51ed-ac80-498a071f0b9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2ex+2ey+ez+3e=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554262} {:answer/id #uuid "c1fe292e-1813-51b6-937f-ba4fbfabb74f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2ex+2ey-\\frac{z}{e}-4e-\\frac{1}{e}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554290}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554290} :answer-field/id #uuid "102d43bf-f5e9-5d2c-bd0c-f23bbb64ece6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6cd59b40-dc86-5174-9cba-78e6f66091cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-86454" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=2y{e}^{x}-{e}^{z}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y{e}^{x}-{e}^{z})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y{e}^{x}-{e}^{z})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2y{e}^{x}-{e}^{z})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2y{e}^{x}\\text{ }i+2{e}^{x}\\text{ }j-{e}^{z}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,-1) & =2(1)e\\text{ }i+2e\\text{ }j-{e}^{-1}k \\\\  & =2e\\,i+2e\\,j-{e}^{-1}k \\\\  & =⟨2e,2e,-\\frac{1}{e}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2e,2e,-\\frac{1}{e}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2ex+2ey-\\frac{z}{e}-4e-\\frac{1}{e} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "fb365c06-0aef-539e-aff8-8e2d2bf57273" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554677}}] :activity/title "Tangent Planes to Level Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553851}]}
